 "brief": {
  "genre": "Orchestral / intimate cinematic drama",
  "mood": "Tender, desperate, bereft",
  "use": "Single continuous story cue for a death scene; no supplied picture or timed hit points.",
  "notes": "48 bars (~134 seconds plus natural tail), 86 BPM, 4/4, one-shot. Bars 1-12 Calm and perfect: relative Gb major, genuine warmth without ominous foreshadowing; establish a singable soulmate motif as a piano/cello dialogue. Bars 13-24 Life and death: sudden threat at 13:1, double-time rhythmic feel at unchanged tempo, Eb minor, escalating urgent struggle, no heroic triumph; terminal rupture at 24:4. Bars 25-32 Loss: near-silence at 25:1 (tails allowed), sparse broken piano, soulmate cello absent, suspended time. Bars 33-44 Realisation: abrupt recognition at 33:1 through recognisable return of opening motif in minor, rise to emotional peak around 39-40, grief rather than renewed action. Bars 45-48 Coda: withdraw to an incomplete, solitary recollection and quiet unresolved final sonority. Last written release by 49:1, 6-second natural tail. Composer owns exact harmony and motif; all other parts follow chord track. Palette: intimate acoustic piano, solo cello, upper and lower ensemble strings, orchestral bass, low orchestral percussion. No vocals. Deliver stereo 48kHz WAV plus MIDI if supported; final output path selected from project render facilities at delivery. Preserve dynamic contrast, target -18 LUFS integrated, ceiling -1 dBTP without crushing peaks."
 },
